+# Daily Grind
+
+Use Node.js 20 or newer. `npm start` serves the homepage and newsletter endpoint
+on port 11222 (override with `PORT`). `npm run build` checks JavaScript syntax;
+there is no compilation step or dependency installation required.
+
+The signup form posts to `/api/newsletter`. Accepted addresses are appended to
+`data/subscribers.jsonl` with a timestamp. Set `NEWSLETTER_FILE` to choose another
+persistent storage path. Keep that file private and persist it across deployments.
+The endpoint records signups; it does not send newsletters or confirmation emails.
+A reverse proxy terminating HTTPS should preserve the original `Host` header.
+
+All responses carry a Content Security Policy. Scripts, styles, and fetch requests
+use this origin only; images may also load from `https://images.unsplash.com`.
+Inline scripts/styles, external form submissions, frames, objects, and base URL
+overrides are blocked. Only the homepage, CSS, and client script are served as
+files; subscriber storage is never a static route.
+
+The form announces success and request failures, retains the address on failure,
+and allows retrying after network errors, blocked requests, or a ten-second timeout.
